{"connection_id": "BC-43fe15142270d44d2351", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.8", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God grows grass", "note": "The commentary links God’s act of bringing forth pasture with a shepherd’s provision; YHWH covers the sky with clouds and makes grass grow on the mountains, naming the growth as God’s work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-336b7ba3b426e7e5448b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.8", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rain makes grass grow on mountains", "note": "God covers the sky, prepares rain, and sprouts grass on the mountains; this connects divine production of grazing land with the commentary's mountain-and-pasture association."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ed0ac0beddd13002fc7a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.9", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Food for animals", "note": "The commentary connects pasture with guarded livestock; God gives animals their food, even young ravens when they cry, extending the provision beyond a human flock."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ff7fcda405f3dfa110cd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.9", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God gives food to beasts", "note": "The creator's provision of food to animals makes explicit the care for livestock that the source reads into pasture."}
{"connection_id": "BC-459cdd40093e67e51f55", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.1", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Personal shepherd and owner", "note": "The commentary says Rab is owner and later notes one who names “his Lord”; David calls YHWH “my shepherd,” making ownership a personal relation of trust."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3667ecb68e241ea3ae99", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.1", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Rab as flock-owner and shepherd", "note": "The psalm names YHWH as the speaker's shepherd, giving the source's Rab who owns and directs the herd a direct divine pastoral frame."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5ae6d8b5fb308fd36a39", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.2", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Green pasture and leading", "note": "The commentary joins the one who guides a flock to protected pasture; YHWH makes the speaker lie down in green pastures and leads him beside waters, furnishing the same pastoral sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bacdad56f310a1106b74", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.2", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "green pastures and resting waters", "note": "The shepherd brings the dependent flock to nourishing pasture and rest, closely matching the commentary's owner who brings the herd to a protected grazing place."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b06d179475441c67449d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.3", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Guidance and correction", "note": "The commentary’s Rab can mean one who sets things right and its guidance image leads the herd; here the shepherd restores the soul and leads in right paths, linking care with moral direction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7bf56df48d78912c93c8", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.3", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restore and guide in right paths", "note": "The same shepherd restores and leads the person on paths; this makes the source's هدى B003 front-leading image part of pastoral care rather than mere travel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8270a36f90e8c0b70c77", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.4", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Protection in danger", "note": "The commentary glosses the shepherd as surrounding and protecting livestock; the speaker fears no evil in the dark valley because YHWH is with him and uses rod and staff to comfort him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-89069bc396c404980007", "ref": "WLC:Ps.28.9", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shepherd and carry God's inheritance forever", "note": "The plea asks God to save, bless, shepherd, and carry his people forever; it makes protective pastoral rule explicitly enduring, relevant to the source's turn from temporary pasture to what lasts."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0b1fe3df3b9eae3b549c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.50.10", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Owner of livestock", "note": "The commentary calls Rab the owner of everything and evokes a herd; God says every forest animal and cattle on a thousand hills are his, giving the ownership claim concrete scope."}
{"connection_id": "BC-722782c24eb5164e13f5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.50.10", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cattle on a thousand hills are mine", "note": "God's claim over cattle supplies a concrete biblical form for the commentary's insistence that Rab is the owner before he is the herd's guide."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ae67fa6e43b85891ebf0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.50.11", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wild herd under divine knowledge", "note": "The commentary includes a wild-cattle herd under the r-b-b word family; God says he knows every bird of the mountains and the creatures of the field are his, extending divine ownership to wild creatures."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ae1ac46bc085879f7e14", "ref": "WLC:Ps.50.12", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Creation belongs to God", "note": "The commentary’s Rab means owner of everything; God says the world and all it contains are his, grounding the pasture scene in universal possession."}
{"connection_id": "BC-45e0378312f6459b5b27", "ref": "WLC:Ps.65.13", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Pastures clothed with flocks", "note": "The commentary presents a pasture brought forth for a herd; the psalm depicts pastures clothed with flocks and valleys covered with grain, adding an image of abundance to divine provision."}
{"connection_id": "BC-06cd6b7e1ab9d1175e38", "ref": "WLC:Ps.65.13", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "pastures clothed with flocks and fields sing", "note": "Pastures are filled with flocks and the fertile landscape shouts and sings; it lets the source's opening praise encompass the very pasture and herd that God causes to thrive."}
{"connection_id": "BC-27e802f712e8027383de", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.20", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Moses and Aaron lead God's people like a flock", "note": "The psalm says God led the people like a flock by Moses and Aaron, giving the commentary's Moses-linked scene a divine owner, human agents, and flock in one verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc6816fcddb5c1815474", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.21", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Moses leads Israel like a flock", "note": "The commentary points to Moses’ pastoral reply to Pharaoh and develops guidance of a herd; the psalm recalls God leading his people like a flock by Moses and Aaron, placing the image in the Exodus story."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d642c0b26431ffeab114", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.52", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads his flock", "note": "The commentary makes the owner, the ones leading ahead, and pasture parts of one scene; God brings Israel out like sheep and leads them through the wilderness, joining divine guidance to flock imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-244d86029414119e653d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.52", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads people as sheep and guides them as flock", "note": "The wilderness exodus is described with both flock-leading and guidance, closely matching the source's single work of owner, guide, and herd."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e36e7dddc40b30b9d1a0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.53", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Safe guidance", "note": "The commentary says the shepherd protects the animals he guides; Israel is led safely here, with the sea overwhelming its enemies, pairing guidance with protection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bfa6fc95839cd8cb5ebd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.71", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "David brought from tending sheep", "note": "The commentary links the shepherd of animals to the ruler of people; God takes David from following nursing ewes to shepherd Jacob, making the transition from literal flock care to leadership explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a6b3a19d82fcd34ea603", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.72", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "David shepherds and guides Israel", "note": "The commentary’s flock leaders guide those behind them and its ruler tends subjects; David shepherds Israel with an upright heart and guides them with skillful hands, uniting care and guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b5f65a3552c2ab6838a7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.72", "target": "sec3", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "David shepherds with integrity and skillful guidance", "note": "David's shepherding is defined by inner integrity and skilled leading, developing the source's claim that pastoral language can describe competent public rule."}
