text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /Volumes/aro/projects/prose_generation/enrichment/bible/work/s087/ehlikitap-images.sol.max.session-20261005/sec3/verdicts.jsonl
+{"connection_id":"BC-83f4fc8e20344d95e17f","ref":"Augustine, Tractates on the Gospel of John 46","status":"unavailable","reason":"Augustine's exposition is absent from this local snapshot; its proposed contrast cannot be checked here.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7651952f11b5633ac15b","ref":"Gospel of Thomas 107","status":"unavailable","reason":"The apocryphal saying is absent from this local snapshot; the distinctive largest-sheep wording is unverified.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ebe96ec10d54323049c6","ref":"Peshitta: John 10:11","status":"unavailable","reason":"The Syriac witness is absent from this local snapshot; its proposed rʿyā wording and cognate claim cannot be checked.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e6de16c4372ae0e14c61","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.9.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul applies the ox law to the wages of human laborers, not to a divine shepherd leading a herd to pasture; the para 14 image gains no distinct point.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.9.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6313a9799fed1c59609e","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.9.7","status":"rejected","reason":"The flock's milk supports Paul's case for a worker's livelihood; it does not discuss pasture grown by God or the herd's protection.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.9.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c8ef7abd5ea4ce307f59","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.9.9","status":"rejected","reason":"The ox is unmuzzled during threshing, a labor-rights example; the claimed pastoral-provision relation shifts away from the page's grazing scene.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.9.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1e31d2606aad4d086319","ref":"SBLGNT:1John.2.17","status":"accepted","reason":"The world passing while the doer of God's will remains is the explicit temporary/enduring contrast invoked at paragraph 16.","paragraphs":[16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1John.2.17","SBLGNT:2Cor.4.18"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-006"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bdb7821ff8941b2ced47","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24","status":"accepted","reason":"Peter explicitly applies withering grass to all flesh and its glory, a Christian interpretation of the transience image.","paragraphs":[16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24","SBLGNT:1Pet.1.25"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-feec494ef4a7b5d11536","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24","status":"accepted","reason":"The grass-withering line grounds the specific mortality extension expressed in the annotation.","paragraphs":[16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24","SBLGNT:1Pet.1.25"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0c80649aaaa56fb81266","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.1.25","status":"accepted","reason":"The immediately following enduring word completes Peter's grass contrast and is distinguished from Isaiah's Hebrew witness.","paragraphs":[16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24","SBLGNT:1Pet.1.25"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7a58f43275d9c9e20c2e","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.2.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Returning to the overseer of souls is an explicitly spiritual restoration; the page's source paragraph treats herd guidance and pasture, already closer in John 10.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-84df5d0edd195c37712c","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.2.25","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse's wandering-souls application adds no specific animal-leading or grazing detail beyond the selected John 10 scene.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-966ad81e1357f8e0168d","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","status":"accepted","reason":"Elders are ordered to shepherd God's flock, an explicit public-leadership application of the paragraph 14 lexical image.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-431861aef79c53187230","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","status":"accepted","reason":"Oversight of God's flock concretely supports the shepherd-ruler sense and is presented with its non-dominating qualification.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-510cf6b96ad1738e9461","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","status":"accepted","reason":"The command not to dominate states a distinct ethical limit on the leaders addressed in 5:2.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-145d66e74e6cb7988397","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse explicitly contrasts domineering with exemplary conduct toward the flock, refining the ruler-shepherd analogy.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1f91c3bda05e3bbed862","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.4","status":"rejected","reason":"The arch-shepherd's future appearance and crown concern Christian reward; the selected 5:2-3 block already states delegated flock oversight without this separate eschatology.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a901dc16d7fb8fb1ee3b","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.5.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Chief-shepherd hierarchy is real in the verse, but its crown-at-appearing point is beyond the commentary's owner, grazing, and watchfulness claims.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-34433067d4349b3a952e","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.4.18","status":"accepted","reason":"Paul explicitly distinguishes transient visible things from enduring unseen things, the paragraph 16 conclusion without the pasture image.","paragraphs":[16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1John.2.17","SBLGNT:2Cor.4.18"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-006"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-84822d5d1fff53c143fb","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.20.28","status":"accepted","reason":"Overseers are charged to shepherd God's acquired assembly, joining delegated leadership and divine ownership.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-cad6be4e08dfcdc400f3","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.20.28","status":"accepted","reason":"Attention to the entire flock and the shepherding charge supply the proposed oversight point.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.5.2","SBLGNT:1Pet.5.3","SBLGNT:Acts.20.28"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-05bdfc07eedfd0aa748b","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.20.29","status":"rejected","reason":"The wolves explain why the Acts overseers must be vigilant, but predator danger is more concretely developed by the selected John 10:12 hired-hand contrast.","paragraphs":[14,15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.20.29"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b7c32c6aa2c675055b28","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.4.11","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse only lists pastors and teachers as offices; it supplies no flock, leading, grazing, or protection action beyond the fuller 1 Peter 5 passage.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.4.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d20a399bab61f5c9ec12","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.13.20","status":"rejected","reason":"The title great shepherd occurs within resurrection and covenant language, without the owner-to-pasture sequence considered in this section.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.13.20"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-19472ae1bd72aba4ac08","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.13.20","status":"rejected","reason":"The Christological covenant title is a later theological application of shepherding; John 10 provides direct flock care and guidance for this paragraph.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.13.20"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-06e6bb85a9028f89663c","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.11","status":"accepted","reason":"The good shepherd's self-giving is a specific protective action, expressed with the contrasting hired hand in the annotation.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f4141a17ea1c25a5b43c","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.11","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek explicitly says the good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep; this defines costly care in John's own scene.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ea984821c0eec472671","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.12","status":"accepted","reason":"The hired man abandons the sheep on seeing a wolf, a precise negative foil to protective ownership.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a8926e0dc6da2d3c1b9f","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.12","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek explicitly says the sheep are not the hireling's own and that he flees, making ownership the operative contrast.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d1d8a03ccba7cc80a297","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.14","status":"accepted","reason":"Jesus' mutual knowledge of his own sheep adds recognition to the protective owner-shepherd contrast.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f315ca91ed8da870c451","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.14","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse names both his knowing the sheep and their knowing him, relevant to the paragraph's personal 'his Lord' wording.","paragraphs":[15],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.11","SBLGNT:John.10.12","SBLGNT:John.10.14"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ba5b7ac955936f7f6cf5","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.28","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse's eternal life and protection from snatching are specific Christian salvation promises; the section's pasture decay is not this flock's ultimate fate.","paragraphs":[15,16],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.28"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a58b6fab8b18394f847f","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.3","status":"accepted","reason":"The shepherd calls his own sheep and brings them out, supplying belonging and guidance in a single scene.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c797c145ca3ff00a6829","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.3","status":"accepted","reason":"The own-sheep and leads-out wording underpins the precise owner-and-leader comparison.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c81c7c1982c80b77900b","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.4","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek says the shepherd goes before them and the sheep follow, exactly the front-leading element.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e85f7320770967ab576f","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.4","status":"accepted","reason":"Walking in front of the flock and its following are explicitly joined, supporting the particular leading image.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2a32fe3aae4c2f2d3f51","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.9","status":"accepted","reason":"The promise that one entering will find pasture completes the chapter's leading-and-belonging scene.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-efef59333cf92b02ddfe","ref":"SBLGNT:John.10.9","status":"accepted","reason":"Pasture is named after safe going in and out, joining protection and grazing in the selected John 10 annotation.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.10.3","SBLGNT:John.10.4","SBLGNT:John.10.9"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a794c28342e93771b353","ref":"SBLGNT:John.21.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Peter's delegated tending is real, but 1 Peter 5:2-3 and Acts 20:28 give this page the fuller public leadership and oversight point.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.21.16"],"annotations":[]}
